ing aesthetic.- Dark charcoal and black background.- Orange accent color for important buttons.- White typography and clean content sections.- Large professional welding hero image.- Modern rounded service cards.- Industrial project photography.- Elegant navigation bar.- Strong visual hierarchy.- Professional spacing and alignment.- Premium typography.- Subtle shadows and smooth transitions.The overall design should look sophisticated, powerful, trustworthy, and internationally competitive.Suggested color palette:- Deep Charcoal: #17191B- Industrial Black: #101214- Steel Grey: #45494D- Pure White: #FFFFFF- Accent Orange: #F26A32- Light Grey: #F1F2F3Use these colors consistently throughout the website.PHASE 3 â€” WEBSITE ARCHITECTUREAfter gathering my requirements, propose a complete website architecture.Recommend the most suitable technology stack supported by the environment.Prefer:- React- Modern CSS or Tailwind CSS- Reusable components- Responsive layouts- Clean project structure- SEO-friendly implementationExplain the architecture before implementation.PHASE 4 â€” WEBSITE DESIGN AND SECTIONSBuild the following sections:1. PREMIUM NAVIGATION BARCreate a stylish navigation bar with:- Logo placeholder on the left.- Home- Services- Projects- About Us- Certifications- Contact- Orange Request a Quote button.Make the navigation responsive and provide a professional mobile menu.2. HERO SECTIONCreate a stunning full-width industrial hero section.Use a high-quality image of a professional welder working with metal in a modern industrial workshop.Include a dark overlay for readable text.Suggested headline:"PRECISION WELDING &amp; METAL FABRICATION EXPERTS"Add a short professional description and two calls to action:- Request a Quote- Explore Our ServicesUse large, bold, premium typography.3. FEATURED SERVICE CARDSCreate three visually attractive service cards:- Structural Welding- Custom Fabrication- Repair &amp; MaintenanceEach card should contain a professional icon, short description, and Learn More link.Use dark backgrounds, rounded corners, white content areas, and subtle hover effects.4. COMPLETE WELDING SOLUTIONSCreate a beautiful white-background section showing different welding services.Include:- MIG &amp; TIG Welding- Steel Fabrication- Aluminum Welding- Pipe Welding- On-site Welding- Industrial RepairsUse clean professional icons and short descriptions.5. PROJECT PORTFOLIOCreate a premium industrial project gallery.Showcase:- Structural steel projects.- Industrial steel frameworks.- Metal gates and grills.- Custom fabrication.- Pipe fabrication.- Welding projects.Use large, high-quality images and elegant image cards.Add category filtering.Allow the business owner to replace sample images with actual workshop photographs.Never claim sample photographs are actual completed customer projects.6. CLIENT TESTIMONIALSCreate a clean testimonial section with attractive cards.Use editable placeholder testimonials.Do not invent real customer identities or verified reviews.7. CERTIFICATIONS AND SAFETYCreate a professional certifications and safety section.Include editable placeholders for certifications and safety standards.Only display actual certifications when supplied by the business owner.8. INDUSTRIAL STATSCreate a modern statistics section with editable values.Possible categories:- Completed Projects- Customer Satisfaction- Years of Experience- Professional ServicesDo not invent statistics. Use placeholders until verified figures are provided.9. CONTACT AND QUOTE SECTIONCreate an attractive contact area with:- Name- Phone Number- Email- Service Type- Project Details- Submit RequestAdd a WhatsApp inquiry button.Make all contact information editable.Do not invent phone numbers or email addresses.10. PROFESSIONAL FOOTERInclude:- Business logo placeholder.- Business description.- Navigation links.- Services.- Contact information.- Social media links.- Copyright.PHASE 5 â€” FUNCTIONALITYThe website must be genuinely functional.Implement:- Working navigation.- Responsive mobile menu.- Functional service links.- Project gallery filters.- Contact form validation.- WhatsApp integration with configurable phone number.- Smooth scrolling.- Interactive buttons.- Accessible navigation.Do not create buttons that look functional but do nothing.If a backend or email service is required, explain the integration requirements and use a secure implementation.PHASE 6 â€” RESPONSIVE DESIGNOptimize the entire website for:- Android phones.- iPhones.- Tablets.- Laptops.- Desktop screens.Mobile responsiveness is extremely important.Ensure:- No horizontal overflow.- Proper image cropping.- Readable typography.- Touch-friendly buttons.- Responsive cards.- Proper mobile navigation.PHASE 7 â€” SEO AND PERFORMANCEImplement:- SEO-friendly titles.- Meta descriptions.- Semantic HTML.- Image alt attributes.- Fast loading.- Optimized images.- Accessibility improvements.- Clean URLs where applicable.- Social sharing metadata.PHASE 8 â€” DEVELOPMENT EXECUTIONFollow this development process:1. First analyze the reference image.2. Ask discovery questions.3. Wait for my answers.4. Propose the design system.5. Propose the architecture.6. Wait for my approval.7. Build the website section by section.8. Test all functionality.9. Fix layout and responsiveness issues.10. Deliver the completed project.Do not generate final code before completing the discovery and planning phases.Do not provide incomplete code, fake functionality, or shortcuts such as "// add code here".FINAL QUALITY REQUIREMENTThe final website must look like a premium international industrial engineering company's website.It should be visually close to the attached reference image while being more polished, modern, professional, and user-friendly.The website must communicate precision, quality, reliability, craftsmanship, and professionalism.The ultimate goal is to create a strong digital identity for a welding and metal fabrication business that can attract customers and build trust worldwide.Start with PHASE 1 only. Ask your discovery questions and wait for my answers before proceeding.</span><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ms-cmark-node></p><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ms-cmark-node><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></ms-console-turn></div><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2464125534="" class="turn ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2464125534="" role="heading" aria-level="3" class="turn-header ng-star-inserted"><button _ngcontent-ng-c2464125534="" class="model-name"> Gemini 3.8 Flash </button><span _ngcontent-ng-c2464125534="" class="circle"></span><span _ngcontent-ng-c2464125534=""><!----><!----> Ran for <span _ngcontent-ng-c2464125534="" class="duration ng-star-inserted">18s</span><!----></span></div><!----><ms-console-assistant-response _ngcontent-ng-c2464125534="" _nghost-ng-c855282918=""><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" class="expansion-panel ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" class="sticky-wrapper"><div _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" class="header"><div _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" class="header-inner"><button _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" class="title" aria-disabled="false"><span _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" aria-hidden="true" class="material-symbols-outlined notranslate"> summarize_auto </span><span _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="">Action history</span><span _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" aria-hidden="true" class="expand-icon material-symbols-outlined notranslate"> chevron_right </span></button><div _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" class="actions"><span _ngcontent-ng-c855282918="" aria-hidden=